17592186415674 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415674 1077 "selection" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415674 1078 #edb/ref 17592186415666 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415674 1079 #uuid "77c94cbf-f9ef-59ad-9086-7c8d91862986" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415675 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415644 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415675 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415647 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415675 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415648 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415675 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415655 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415675 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415660 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415675 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415675 1077 "selection" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415675 1078 #edb/ref 17592186415647 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415675 1079 #uuid "9bc8f0e0-f5cb-5cee-aa30-efe616caf6e2" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415676 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415667 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415676 1069 "q-124313" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415676 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415676 1071 "![](images/fb/fbc6ddf87d5f5502db656242222dca27fb33ded5d3bdcf372b70ef10eda07624.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along a three-quarter circle of radius $3,$ traversed from the point $(-1,-3)$ to the point $(-4,0),$ shown above." 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415676 1072 #uuid "19c93f12-207e-5d48-9d03-3dc16bfb7738" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415676 1074 "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=-4$ and ${x}_{1}=-1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=(-4)-(-1)=-3.\n$$" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415677 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415672 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415677 1069 "q-124187" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415677 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415677 1071 "If ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=17,$ ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=7,$ and ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=5,$ calculate ${\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}.$" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415677 1072 #uuid "28b25a72-e404-5d69-993b-a9b2c8d9ba39" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415677 1074 "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 17 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+5-{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 17 & =-7+5-{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 19 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-19.\n$$" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415678 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415675 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415678 1069 "q-124183" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415678 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415678 1071 "If ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=14$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-6,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415678 1072 #uuid "41a5f2bb-63fd-5596-b20f-47e35c05d2ec" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415678 1074 "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =14-(-6) \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415679 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415669 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415679 1069 "q-124290" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415679 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415679 1071 "![](images/4d/4d1c20f44c7a092275f200737813e11c762e1f3e80ba22ded29b41731e22472e.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is the path comprising of two line segments, as shown above." 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415679 1072 #uuid "81ff799c-e275-561c-accd-b7005d2a330b" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415679 1074 "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=4$ and ${x}_{1}=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=4-0=4.\n$$" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415680 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415673 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415680 1069 "q-124300" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415680 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415680 1071 "![](images/71/71620d1e3e6691ef6c91382665fd258891984b1e32aeaec122663d65c1ca5b1b.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment between the points $(-3,-1)$ to the point $(1,3),$ as shown above." 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415680 1072 #uuid "a19a3e84-b3b7-545b-90bc-54d947e5986c" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415680 1074 "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=1$ and ${x}_{1}=-3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=1-(-3)=4.\n$$" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415681 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415671 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415681 1069 "q-124306" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415681 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415681 1071 "![](images/05/05b76357203cf2d7ef38b4bfa8daa9e0ce21b248f150e1a2d516f1a4c4e5bef3.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along a quarter circle of radius $1,$ traversed from the point $(0,2)$ to the point $(1,1),$ shown above." 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415681 1072 #uuid "c4b4530c-a5d4-5bda-8a1d-c3d8365018f1" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415681 1074 "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=1$ and ${x}_{1}=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=1-0=1.\n$$" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415682 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415674 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415682 1069 "q-124329" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415682 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415682 1071 "![](images/77/77c069c4b4306b3337a44ddfc53ecd4d727e78da09d77d61e84fc01d3b30c302.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the closed path along the square of \nside $2,$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415682 1072 #uuid "caee1f70-9af3-5daf-82bf-4723f96ead82" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true] [17592186415682 1074 "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, the initial and terminal points are the same (since the path is closed and is traversed only once). Therefore, ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$ and we have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$" 13194139534243 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-01e4d0b1-3d49-5ae5-b65b-8dbe801177f5" 17592186415622 "answer-05561efb-810b-5987-b7e5-1cc8fd5d9c6a" 17592186415623 "answer-105bce54-4026-504a-aebc-d3aeaf976b6a" 17592186415624 "answer-1